WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.160
If the neural tube does not close, part of the brain or spinal cord stays open.

2
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.440
Failure at the head end causes anencephaly.

3
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.980
At the lower end, it causes open spina bifida.

4
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.980
These defects can be fatal or cause weakness or paralysis.

5
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.440
Closure happens by the end of about the fourth week after fertilization, often

6
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.560
before a woman knows she is pregnant.

7
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.900
Folic acid taken before conception lowers the risk of many of these defects.

8
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:37.983
The brain and spinal cord begin as the neural plate, a flat sheet on the embryo’s

9
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:40.283
back. It narrows and lengthens.

10
00:00:41.163 --> 00:00:44.723
It creases at hinge points, and its edges rise as neural folds.

11
00:00:45.643 --> 00:00:46.803
The folds meet and fuse.

12
00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:50.523
The tube separates from the skin, which seals over it.

13
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.817
In anencephaly, exposed brain tissue degenerates.

14
00:00:55.737 --> 00:00:58.517
Affected babies are stillborn or die soon after birth.

15
00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:03.017
In one form of open spina bifida, the cord lies in the lesion.

16
00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:07.797
Weakness or paralysis and loss of bladder and bowel control are common.

17
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.120
Randomized trials tested prevention.

18
00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.880
In women with a previous affected pregnancy, folic acid started before conception

19
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.540
cut recurrence by about 72 percent.

20
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.780
A Hungarian trial found no affected pregnancies with a multivitamin containing folic

21
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.740
acid, against six in the comparison group.

22
00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.720
That supports prevention of a first occurrence.

23
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.800
But that trial alone could not credit folic acid by itself.

24
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.353
Now consider one route to closure failure.

25
00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:44.333
Convergent extension narrows the plate as cells push between side neighbors.

26
00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:47.873
Planar cell polarity gives them a shared direction.

27
00:01:48.653 --> 00:01:51.433
If the plate stays too wide, the folds cannot meet.

28
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:57.477
In frog embryos, researchers disrupted Dishevelled signaling at the plate’s midline.

29
00:01:58.357 --> 00:01:59.357
The plate stayed wide.

30
00:02:00.157 --> 00:02:03.497
The folds still rose and moved inward, but the tube stayed open.

31
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.520
Disrupting the sides instead left closure intact.

32
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.760
Under those conditions, the signal was needed at the midline, where narrowing sets

33
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.860
the distance. In the loop-tail mouse, the midline failed to extend before folding,

34
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.460
and closure never started.

35
00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:21.643
There are other routes.

36
00:02:22.603 --> 00:02:28.043
Diabetes before pregnancy and valproic acid in early pregnancy raise the risk of

37
00:02:28.043 --> 00:02:33.803
spina bifida. Most mothers of affected babies are not folate deficient by ordinary

38
00:02:33.803 --> 00:02:37.423
tests. How folate prevents defects is not settled.

39
00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:41.883
Its benefit is clear: lower risk, with some defects still occurring.
